Chapter: FbProbe
  cites Works chapter MetalLadder
  cites Works chapter GopHandoff

 Does a payload's framebuffer write reach the PANEL, or only its own memory?

 It paints WHITE and holds, and prints the handoff geometry beside it. The
 answer is not the printed line: `ladder-paint` reads its own store back, which
 succeeds whenever the address is mapped at all, so the only honest reading is
 the screenshot. Run it under `codex-vm -uefi -gop -screenshot` and compare the
 BMP against `painted=`.

 We say:

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Integer = act
    p <- ladder-pass 1 ladder-white ladder-red
    print-line-uni ("FBPROBE painted=" & show p & " base=" & show (boot-fb-base 0) & " w=" & show (boot-fb-w 0) & " h=" & show (boot-fb-h 0) & " stride=" & show (boot-fb-stride 0))
    ladder-hold ladder-white
  end
